From 5b4fbe015cfaa9e09b85f37641fbd7552eba0da8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:29:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: bridge: samsung-dsim: use the exynos7870 PLL operating
 point

The exynos7870 driver data carries m_max = 125, min_freq = 500 and
max_freq = 1500, the same numbers as the exynos5433 entry a few lines
above, from which they were copied. They do not describe this PLL.

samsung_dsim_pll_find_pms() checks m against m_min/m_max and the VCO
frequency, m * fin / p, against min_freq/max_freq. On gtaxlwifi, fin is
26 MHz and the panel asks for 979.33 MHz: with those limits the only
solution the search can accept is p 3, m 113, s 0, which runs the VCO at
979.33 MHz. The vendor never searches at all - its driver reads the
values from the device tree, with a comment saying they come from the
PLL calculation tool and are to be used as given - and for this panel
the device tree says timing,pms = <3 226 1>, a VCO of 1958.7 MHz. Same
output frequency, twice the VCO, and the low one is a point Samsung does
not use on this SoC.

The exact limits of this PLL are not published, so pick them so that the
search reproduces the vendor's values: with a VCO between 1000 and 2100
MHz and m up to the width of its register field, p 3, m 113, s 0 falls
below the minimum and the search returns p 3, m 226, s 1. The M field is
ten bits wide (PLL_EN is bit 23, P starts at bit 13, M at bit 3), so 226
fits.

The panel has been coming back from a short screen off with horizontal
stripes at line pitch on about one wake-up in fifty, with the init
sequence now byte identical to the vendor table and the same power
sequencing; the clock the whole link is built on is the part that had
not been checked.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c
index 32c047e967..1af93c855c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/samsung-dsim.c
@@ -626,7 +626,7 @@ static const struct samsung_dsim_driver_data exynos7870_dsi_driver_data = {
 	.clklane_stop_only = 1,
 	.clk_data = exynos7870_clk_bulk_data,
 	.num_clks = ARRAY_SIZE(exynos7870_clk_bulk_data),
-	.max_freq = 1500,
+	.max_freq = 2100,
 	.wait_for_hdr_fifo = 1,
 	.hdr_fifo_empty_bit = 10,
 	.hdr_fifo_full_bit = 11,
@@ -647,8 +647,8 @@ static const struct samsung_dsim_driver_data exynos7870_dsi_driver_data = {
 	.pll_fin_min = 6,
 	.pll_fin_max = 12,
 	.m_min = 41,
-	.m_max = 125,
-	.min_freq = 500,
+	.m_max = 1023,
+	.min_freq = 1000,
 };
 
 static const struct samsung_dsim_driver_data imx8mm_dsi_driver_data = {
-- 
